            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "These are mapping to https://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/Redundancy.v1_5_0.json from \n\n                \"MaxSupportedInGroup\": {\n                    \"description\": \"The maximum number of devices supported in this redundancy group.\",\n                    \"longDescription\": \"This property shall contain the maximum number of devices allowed in the redundancy group.\",\n                    \"readonly\": true,\n                    \"type\": [\n                        \"integer\",\n                        \"null\"\n                    ],\n                    \"versionAdded\": \"v1_4_0\"\n                },\n                \"MinNeededInGroup\": {\n                    \"description\": \"The minimum number of devices needed for this group to be redundant.\",\n                    \"longDescription\": \"This property shall contain the minimum number of functional devices needed in the redundancy group for the current redundancy mode to be fault tolerant.\",\n                    \"readonly\": true,\n                    \"type\": [\n                        \"integer\",\n                        \"null\"\n                    ],\n                    \"versionAdded\": \"v1_4_0\"\n                },\n\nI assume?\n\nIn a simple Active and Backup design, is 2 and 2 what these values will be?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "From the Redfish mockup of this case I expect this would be minimum:1; maximum:2.\n\nhttps://redfish.dmtf.org/redfish/mockups/v1/1590\n(See Managers->Switch1)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you add into the commit the redfish schema this is for?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/BMC/Redundancy.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "While it may just get converted to zero here, 'false' probably isn't the ideal default value for a property of type 'size'."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/BMC/Redundancy.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "Good catch! I meant to remove the default values. I've removed them now."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/BMC/Redundancy.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 56,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "In latest patch set I added back default for the RedundancyMinimum property since it is a required property. (I added it using an integer though!)"
                }
            ],
